      "body": "Fixes #43395\n\n## Summary\n\nComfyUI-mode Flux loading always set `guidance_embeds=True`, assuming every checkpoint has `guidance_in.*` weights. FLUX.1-schnell checkpoints don't have these, so the model gets a guidance embedder that never gets populated, and strict loading fails:\n\n```\nValueError: New parameter 'time_text_embed.guidance_embedder.linear_1.weight' is not supported...\n```\n\nNow `guidance_embeds` is set based on whether the checkpoint actually has `guidance_in.in_layer.weight`, same as ComfyUI does. The skip logic in `_convert_weights` was already there for this but was never reachable until now.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Reproduced the error with a synthetic schnell-shaped checkpoint (no `guidance_in.*`) on CPU before the fix.\n- [x] Added `test_comfyui_flux_guidance_embeds_follows_checkpoint_keys` and `test_comfyui_flux_schnell_checkpoint_loads_without_guidance_embedder` to `test_comfyui_profile.py` — fail on old code, pass with the fix.\n- [x] Ran `test_comfyui_profile.py` and sibling `test_comfyui_*` tests, all green.\n- [x] Loaded the real `black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-schnell` checkpoint through `FluxPipeline(comfyui_mode=True)` on an A100 — loads cleanly (11.89B params), no guidance embedder created.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37957304582](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37957304582)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37957304109](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37957304109)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37957304438](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37957304438)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
